5 Deployment Strategies Every DevOps Engineer Should Know

1. Deploy in Place
Impact if Failed: Downtime
Deploy Time: 1x
Zero Downtime: No
DNS Change Required: No
Rollback: Re-deploy
Code Deployed To: Existing instances

2. Rolling Deployment
Impact if Failed: Single batch impacted
Deploy Time: 2x
Zero Downtime: Yes
DNS Change Required: No
Rollback: Re-deploy
Code Deployed To: Existing instances

3. Immutable Deployment
Impact if Failed: Minimal
Deploy Time: 4x
Zero Downtime: Yes
DNS Change Required: No
Rollback: Re-deploy
Code Deployed To: New instances

4. Traffic Splitting
Impact if Failed: Minimal
Deploy Time: 4x
Zero Downtime: Yes
DNS Change Required: No
Rollback: Re-route traffic and terminate new instances
Code Deployed To: New instances

5. Blue/Green Deployment
Impact if Failed: Minimal
Deploy Time: 4x
Zero Downtime: Yes
DNS Change Required: Yes
Rollback: Switch back to old environment
Code Deployed To: New instances
